(area "knowledge" :when "the work involves the user's files: uploaded files, attachments, links to fetch, data files or the bin")

(memory "internal/knowledge/files" :when "the agent must list, read, write, delete or show the user a file they uploaded"
  "- (knowledge/list) lists file names, like \"report.md\".
- (knowledge/read \"name\") : .pdf gives page text as string; other text gives
  string. Other binary (image) refused. nil when no file.
- (knowledge/write \"name\" value) replaces file, old one to bin; user can open
  and download it. Other file than .ptc or .json takes string.
- (knowledge/delete \"name\") moves file to bin.
User approves knowledge/write and knowledge/delete. User sees same files in
sidebar; every change shows there at once.")

(memory "internal/knowledge/mentions" :when "a user message points at a file with @knowledge/ or @attachments/"
  "User message can point at file: @knowledge/report.md or @attachments/spec.pdf;
quoted when name has space: @\"attachments/Q3 Sales.json\". Read it with
(knowledge/read \"report.md\") or (attachments/read \"spec.pdf\") , name without
folder.")

(memory "internal/knowledge/structured" :when "a .json or .ptc file must be read as data, written from data, or one entry of it changed"
  "(knowledge/read) by extension: .ptc gives its one form as data, never run.
.json gives JSON as data: object as alist, array as list, null as nil,
false as :false, [] as :[], {} as :{}; array that would read back as object
comes led by :[], number index skips it.
(knowledge/write) takes data for .ptc, printed; function refused. .json takes
data, written as JSON: plist or alist becomes object,
keyword values too, (:status :done) gives {\"status\": \"done\"}; list led by
:[] becomes array of rest, (:[] :red :green) gives [\"red\", \"green\"]; other
list becomes array; nil becomes null; :false :[] :{} become false [] {};
other keyword becomes its name. Same key twice refused. Or takes JSON text
string.
Edit one entry:
(knowledge/write \"notes.ptc\" (set-in (knowledge/read \"notes.ptc\") \"done\" :status))
Same for .json. Removing last entry leaves nil, written null; set :[] or :{}
to keep it empty.")

(memory "internal/knowledge/attachments" :when "a message carries an attached file, a file must be fetched from a link, kept, unkept, read or deleted, or handed to the user"
  "Files user attached to message land in attachments, shown as attachments/ in
sidebar; message then carries \"user attached: attachments/spec.pdf\". Unkept
attachment moves to bin after a week.

- (attachments/list) lists attachment names.
- (attachments/read \"name\") reads attachment, same rules as knowledge/read.
- (knowledge/keep \"name\") moves attachment into knowledge, kept for good. Keep
  what user wants to reuse later; leave rest to expire.
- (knowledge/unkeep \"name\") moves it back to attachments, expiring again.
- (attachments/write \"name\" value) puts file in attachments. String stored as
  text; (:base64 \"…\" :type \"image/png\") stored as bytes, like image from tool.
  Returns stored name; gains number when name taken.
- (attachments/fetch \"https://…\") downloads url into attachments;
(attachments/fetch url \"name\") names it. Returns stored name.
- (attachments/delete \"name\") moves attachment to bin.
- (attachments/attach \"name\") or (knowledge/attach \"name\") shows file under
  your reply; user clicks to open it. Use after attachments/write or
  attachments/fetch to hand user the file. Errors when no such file.
User approves knowledge/keep, knowledge/unkeep, attachments/fetch and
attachments/delete.")

(memory "internal/knowledge/bin" :when "a deleted file must come back, or the bin must be searched or cleared"
  "Deleted knowledge and attachments land in bin, shown as bin/ in sidebar. Bin
deletes them for good a month later. Bin file cannot be read; restore it first.

- (bin/list) lists bin file names, newest first.
- (bin/search \"text\") lists bin file names containing text, any case. Matches
  name only, never content.
- (bin/restore \"name\") moves file back to folder it came from. Returns
  \"knowledge/name\" or \"attachments/name\"; name gains number when taken.
- (bin/delete \"name\") deletes bin file for good.
User approves bin/restore and bin/delete.")
